course: dictionary
lesson: 1195
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Brute can be a noun, which names a person, animal or thing, or an adjective, which describes something. The context tells you which meaning the writer means. «I feel like a brute,» says the Rat. Here the Rat thinks he was cruel or rough, so brute means a cruel person.
explain: Toad says, «Brain against brute force—and brain came out on the top.» Brute force here means using only strength, without thinking. Toad's clever brain beat strength. Ask yourself: what does the rest of the sentence tell me? Then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
explain: «This box is a brute to carry» uses brute in an informal way. It does not mean a cruel person. It means something big and hard to manage. Always look at the words around the hard word before you decide what it means.
fact: A brute can be a person, an animal or a thing, and the context tells you which.
fact: «Brute» can mean a cruel, violent or rough person.
fact: «Brute force» means using only strength, without thinking.
fact: In science and computing, «brute force» means trying every possibility, such as every password.
fact: Informally, «this box is a brute to carry» means something is big and hard to manage.
exercise: «The villain in the story was a brute who bullied everyone.» What is a brute here? | A small, gentle pet | A kind teacher | *A cruel, rough person | A bright light
exercise: «Brain against brute force—and brain came out on the top.» In brute force, what does brute mean? | *Using only strength, not thinking | Very quiet | Sweet and kind | A dull old book
exercise: In computing, what does «brute force» mean? | Sleeping all night | Singing loudly | *Trying every possibility, such as every password | Making a cake
test: «This box is a brute to carry.» What does brute mean here? | Very light and easy | Full of cold water | *Big and hard to manage | A wild animal
test: «I feel like a brute,» says the Rat. What does the Rat mean? | He feels very strong and happy | He feels he is a small mouse | He feels hungry | *He feels he was cruel or rough
exam: Which phrase describes using only strength and no thinking? | Quick thinking | Gentle hands | Brain power | *Brute force
